      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's disheartening when well-intentioned advice feels so thin and completely misaligned with what you're actually feeling. This deep, pervasive exhaustion you're describing is a serious kind of emotional weight, and it's not a self-failing. If those immediate connections aren't helping, please consider seeking a mental health professional who is deeply experienced in existential distress, as they can offer a different, more in-depth form of support.",
      "source": "target",
